# iMessage via BlueBubbles HTTP relay.
#
# IMPORTANT: There is no pure-cloud iMessage API. Apple does not expose one.
# BlueBubbles is the standard community workaround — it runs on a macOS host
# that is signed into iMessage and exposes the local message database + send
# queue as an HTTP API.
#
# Install BlueBubbles Server: https://bluebubbles.app
# Docs:                       https://docs.bluebubbles.app
# API reference:              https://documenter.getpostman.com/view/765844/UV5RnfwM
#
# Step-by-step:
#  1. Install BlueBubbles Server on a Mac that's signed into iMessage.
#  2. Set a Server Password in the BlueBubbles UI (Settings → Server).
#  3. Expose the server: either tunnel via ngrok / Cloudflare Tunnel, run on
#     a machine reachable from the agent's host, or keep both on the same
#     private network.
#  4. (Recommended) In the BlueBubbles UI → Settings → Webhooks, add a webhook
#     pointing at <your-server>/webhooks/imessage subscribed to `new-message`.
#     Without webhooks, you must poll /api/v1/message — webhooks are strongly
#     preferred.

# Base URL of the BlueBubbles Server (no trailing path), e.g.
#   http://192.168.1.42:1234
#   https://bluebubbles.example.com
BLUEBUBBLES_SERVER_URL=

# Server password set in the BlueBubbles UI. Used both as the auth query-param
# on outbound calls and as the HMAC key for verifying inbound webhook
# signatures (when webhook signing is enabled in BlueBubbles).
BLUEBUBBLES_PASSWORD=
